              ],
              "content": "Do you know?"
            }
          ],
          "image_source": "images/page_8_image_1.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.259,
            0.101,
            0.755,
            0.225
          ],
          "content": "Some seeds of flowering plants, like Coleus and Petunia, require light to germinate. Covering these seeds with soil inhibits their sprouting. Seeds of flowering plants, like Calendula and Zinnia, need darkness to germinate. These seeds should be covered with sufficient soil."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.259,
            0.744,
            0.342
          ],
          "content": "In the Chapter ‘Mindful Eating: A Path to a Healthy Body’, you have learnt that human beings need a balanced diet for good health and proper growth. Similarly, plants too need favourable conditions and nutrients"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.341,
            0.576,
            0.402
          ],
          "content": "for their proper growth and development. What other conditions do you think would affect seed germination?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.402,
            0.575,
            0.525
          ],
          "content": "In Activity 10.1, what are the characteristics of living beings which made you place plants in living beings? Do plants show growth in Activity 10.2? Are there any other characteristics of living beings that these plants show?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.63,
            0.359,
            0.808,
            0.444
          ],
          "content": "**How would you now categorise a seed, as living or non-living?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.525,
            0.699,
            0.568
          ],
          "content": "Let us study another characteristic that can be seen clearly in plants—growth and movement."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.579,
            0.611,
            0.604
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "10.3 Growth and Movement in Plants"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.614,
            0.744,
            0.719
          ],
          "content": "How do plants respond to sunlight? Does sunlight affect the direction of growth of different parts of plants? In which direction would the root and shoot of a plant grow and move if the plant is placed inverted? How would you **design** an activity to find answers to these questions?"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.728,
            0.41,
            0.751
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Activity 10.3: Let us design"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.76,
            0.744,
            0.802
          ],
          "content": " Take some bean or gram seeds and allow them to germinate on a moist cloth or a moist tissue paper."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.806,
            0.744,
            0.847
          ],
          "content": " Let them germinate until each of them develop into a seedling having a small root and a small shoot."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.852,
            0.743,
            0.893
          ],
          "content": " Now, take three glass beakers or tumblers, and label them as A, B and C."
        },
        {
          "type": "aside_text",
          "bbox": [
            0.88,
            0.705,
            0.918,
            0.87
          ],
          "content": "Characteristics Living Creatures: Exploring their"
